{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788353439,"nonce":"w/JZ2kwj4Ou4oJIWlMDI3D05Hy8=","message":"**MERGED, NOT YET CLOSED — orchestrator verification, repair round 2026-09-02.** Branch `fix/eef837a-bill-filter`, 8 commits, fast-forwarded to `main` at `0ed0840`; assembly rebuilt on `main` as the standalone `4997d9a`. **Held `state:doing` pending the bench**, because this issue's acceptance ends in \"a starving colony with corpses in reach actually eats\" and no bench has run.\n\n\nI did not take the worker's word for this. Every number below I re-derived from `RUNS/m1-20260901/saves/` and the game's own defs.\n\n**1. `bill-add` was never broken.** The issue's headline is that the new bill's filter matched nothing. `day-46.rws` — the day the run created that bill — holds it at `loadID 6` with the `ingredientFilter` **present** and **115 `Corpse_*` defs**, `Corpse_Human` absent, zero mechanoid or drone corpses. That is exactly `ButcherCorpseFlesh.defaultIngredientFilter`, which is `CorpsesAnimal`:\n\n```xml\n\u003cdefaultIngredientFilter\u003e\u003ccategories\u003e\u003cli\u003eCorpsesAnimal\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/categories\u003e\u003c/defaultIngredientFilter\u003e\n```\n\nThe filter was correct from the moment the bill was created, and correct all run.\n\n**2. `bill-set` did persist.** `day-66.rws` `loadID 8` holds **127** entries with `Corpse_Human` now allowed — the edit survived the save. What was wrong was the *arithmetic*: the verb reported 39 defs added over a base of 115, i.e. 154, and the save holds 127. **27 evaporated**, and they are exactly what the recipe's fixed filter excludes:\n\n```xml\n\u003cdisallowedCategories\u003e\u003cli\u003eCorpsesMechanoid\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli MayRequire=\"…Odyssey\"\u003eCorpsesDrone\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/disallowedCategories\u003e\n```\n\nHuman corpses survived; mechanoid corpses did not. So item 2 is a REAL defect, but its size is 27, not 39, and it is a reporting defect rather than a persistence one.\n\n\n```xml\n\u003cfixedIngredientFilter\u003e\n  \u003cspecialFiltersToDisallow\u003e\u003cli\u003eAllowRotten\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/specialFiltersToDisallow\u003e\n\u003c/fixedIngredientFilter\u003e\n\u003cinterruptIfIngredientIsRotting\u003etrue\u003c/interruptIfIngredientIsRotting\u003e\n```\n\n`ThingDefGenerator_Corpses` sets `daysToRotStart = 2.5f` on every generated corpse def — **150,000 ticks**. `day-62.rws` holds the corpse the issue calls fresh:\n\n```\nCorpse_WildBoar  pos=(114,0,138)  rotProg=183767.172  forbidden=false\n```\n\n`(114,138)` is the butcher spot's own cell, the exact cell the issue quotes. `183,767 \u003e 150,000`, so it was **rotting**, and the recipe's fixed filter disallows rotten ingredients. All six corpses on the map that day: two at 183k and 188k, one at 203k, one at 794k, one at 1,099k — and a single fresh deer at `rotProg 137`, sixty cells from the base at `(89,26)`.\n\n**The issue reads \"fresh wild boar corpse (hp 95%)\". Hit points are not rot.** A corpse at 95% hp can be days past rot start, and nothing in the observation surface said so. That is the real signal gap, and it is worse than the one filed: the colony had roughly a 48-hour window per kill and was never told the clock existed.\n\n\n`bills` never emitted a key named `filter`. The key is `ingredient_filter`, written inside a bare try/catch as the last statement of the bill line — a throw left it **absent**, while `FilterSummary.Build` returns **null** for a null filter. Absent and null render identically in the envelope. The run chased a healthy filter for its last twenty days because of that conflation, which is precisely this issue's acceptance item 3 and is now `filter_state` (`published|empty|absent|unavailable`).\n\n\n- **Item 1** — proven false as a defect, and now published as an assertion (`filter_defs` vs `recipe_default_defs`) so it cannot silently regress.\n- **Item 2** — real at size 27; `bill-set` now passes parent-rejected defs through the game's own `exceptedDefs` parameter, reports `defs_delta` as the delta that *survives a save*, and `defs_withheld` for what does not.\n- **Item 3** — `filter_state` shipped.\n- **Item 4 / `d9d6c12`** — `BillWatch` samples `nextTickToSearchForIngredients` every 250 ticks; `asleep-will-retry` and `asleep-no-matching-ingredient` are distinct words.\n- **Item 5** — `accept/eef837a-bill-filter.py` exists; **phases 1-6 and 8 have NOT been run** and need the bench.\n\n\n- **No bench was touched.** Every live behaviour of `bill-add`, `bill-set`, `bills`, the sleep counter, and \"the colony eats\" is unproven against a running game.\n- **The rotten-corpse rejection has not been observed live.** It is proved from the def and from the save, not from a running bill.\n- `BillWatch`'s per-tick cost was not measured on a 38-mod bench.\n- The `bills` ingredient scan budget (2000 things) is a guess bounded by the map's stock, not a measurement.\n\nOrchestrator checks re-run independently: `dotnet build -c Release` on the branch and again on `main` (0 warnings, 0 errors); `accept/eef837a-bill-filter.py --selftest` -\u003e **28/28**, including 9.17-9.22 which prove the suite's own helpers FAIL on an absent key rather than passing on `eq(..., None)`.","files":null}]}